CSI: Wiami Update #2 @everyone  

Greetings Wilders,

Following on from yesterday’s update about a small number of newly minted duplicate Wilder Wheels available on OpenSea, we are pleased to report that we have resolved the issue and will work with the handful of community members affected on a compensation plan.  

  Our investigations identified that a malicious actor was minting on the zNS subdomain system mirroring the same metadata as a very small number of existing domains in zNS. 

The community can be reassured that all subdomains and duplicate items have been burned and the collection integrity has been restored with no impact on rarity or collection size.  

We can also guarantee that there were no issues with the integrity of the smart contracts or code supporting the minting process and the subdomain settings have been updated to prevent this from occurring in the future. 

  In true Wilder Spirit we stand by our community and take care of those affected. Anyone who purchased a duplicate item has the option for receiving their ETH back from their purchase or receiving a randomly minted Crib from our next building launching in Little Meow in the near future. If you were one of the few citizens affected by this - please contact us at info@wilderworld.com. 

  We also want to give a big shout out to the citizens who were quick to act! 

